@event hs_dumont_letter
# en: A Letter From the North
title [586de4] = 来自北境的信
# en: Kael finds you in the library and puts a letter on the table between you without a word. Black-star seal, broken. One line, in a beautiful hand: "I will be at the lake for the Blossom moon. Be there, my son, and bring your friend." It's signed "Mother".{seen(kael_letter_home) > 0: It's her answer to the one he rewrote eleven times.|} His hands are shaking. "She has never come south," he says. "She has never once called me that."
text [527864] = 凯尔在图书馆找到你，一言不发地把一封信放在你们之间的桌上。黑星封蜡，已经拆开。只有一行字，笔迹很美：“花潮之月，我会在湖边。到场吧，我的儿子，带上你的朋友。”署名是“母亲”。{seen(kael_letter_home) > 0: 这是她对那封他改写了十一遍的信的回复。|}他的手在发抖。“她从来没到过南方，”他说，“她从来没这样叫过我。”
# en: A pale young man holding a letter sealed with a black star at arm's length, as if it might bite, frost creeping up the paper from his fingers.
scene [8ef001] = 一个苍白的年轻人把一封黑星封蜡的信远远拿开，好像它会咬人，霜从他的指尖沿着信纸往上爬。
# en: Burn it together
opt.left.label [be972d] = 一起烧掉它
# en: He'll remember who held the match.
opt.left.hint [c0e4af] = 他会记得是谁划的火柴。
# en: You hold it over a candle between you until the black star curls. The flame burns blue, then white, then out, and leaves frost on the candlestick. "She'll know," Kael says. "Good." It's the most like his sister you've ever heard him sound.
opt.left.say.1 [df36cd] = 你们俩把它举在蜡烛上，直到那颗黑星卷曲起来。火焰先是蓝色，然后变白，然后熄灭，在烛台上留下一层霜。“她会知道的，”凯尔说，“很好。”这是你听过的他最像他妹妹的一次。
# en: Keep it. Know your enemy.
opt.right.label [f75413] = 留着它。知己知彼。
# en: Useful. He won't like it.
opt.right.hint [7aa19d] = 有用。他不会喜欢。
# en: You fold it into your notes. Kael watches you do it and says nothing, which is worse than if he had. That night you read the line again by lamplight. The handwriting is beautiful, and patient, and very sure of itself.
opt.right.say.1 [f292cb] = 你把它折好夹进笔记里。凯尔看着你这么做，什么也没说，这比说了还糟。那天夜里你借着灯光又读了一遍那行字。笔迹很美，很耐心，也非常笃定。

@event hs_go_down_early
# en: Before They're Ready
title [6f3947] = 趁他们还没准备好
# en: The lake is freezing in circles tonight, and the key in your pocket is so cold it burns. The Dumonts' mother is coming for the Blossom moon. Her circle isn't ready yet, and neither is the headmistress's. If you went down tonight you'd catch them all unready, and you'd have only the ones who promised you beside you.
text [c7fd4b] = 今晚湖面一圈一圈地冻结，你口袋里的钥匙冷得发烫。杜蒙夫人会在花潮之月到来。她的圈子还没准备好，院长的也还没有。如果你今晚下去，就能趁所有人都没准备好时抓住他们，而你身边只会有那些向你许过诺的人。
# en: A frozen lakeshore at night, a student holding a black star-shaped key up against the moon, a boathouse door ajar behind them.
scene [a4e8ee] = 夜晚结冰的湖岸，一个学生把一把星形的黑钥匙举向月亮，身后船屋的门半开着。
# en: Go down tonight
opt.left.label [7e7ce0] = 今晚就下去
# en: The Night, now. Only the allies who promised come.
opt.left.hint [8490b2] = 那一夜，就是现在。只有许过诺的同伴会来。
# en: You walk down to the boathouse without telling anyone. As you lift the latch, the whole lake behind you goes white in one breath, from shore to shore, and somewhere under it a bell begins to toll.
opt.left.say.1 [e3ef7f] = 你没告诉任何人，独自走向船屋。你抬起门闩时，身后的整片湖在一口气间变白，从这岸到那岸，冰下某处，一口钟开始鸣响。
# en: Wait for the Blossom moon
opt.right.label [4f1efa] = 等到花潮之月
# en: Everyone who'd stand with you will be there. So will everyone against you.
opt.right.hint [dec936] = 所有愿意与你并肩的人都会在。所有与你为敌的人也是。
# en: You stand on the shore until your feet are numb, then go back up to bed. The ice creaks after you all the way. Not yet.
opt.right.say.1 [fc9e35] = 你在岸边站到脚都冻麻了，然后回去睡觉。冰一路在你身后咯吱作响。还不是时候。
